{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"BIT-sqlite-2026-119374","published":"2026-11-17T11:59:57.660Z","modified":"2026-11-17T13:30:14.576768436Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-119374"],"summary":"SQLite before 3.54.0 Heap Buffer Overflow via FTS5 fts5DoSecureDelete()","details":"SQLite before 3.54.0 built with FTS5 contains a heap buffer overflow in fts5DoSecureDelete() that allows attackers to write past the leaf page buffer via crafted footer key offsets. Attackers can supply a database file with a corrupted FTS5 index that, when deleted from with secure-delete enabled, corrupts heap memory and crashes the application.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"sqlite","ecosystem":"Bitnami","purl":"pkg:bitnami/sqlite"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.54.0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/bitnami/vulndb/tree/main/data/sqlite/BIT-sqlite-2026-119374.json"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V4","score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X"}]}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/sqlite-fts5-securedel"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/sqlite/sqlite"},{"type":"FIX","url":"https://github.com/sqlite/sqlite/blob/version-3.53.4/ext/fts5/fts5_index.c#L5525"},{"type":"FIX","url":"https://github.com/sqlite/sqlite/commit/d9de6eedbe918c074c7556400fa21df5960704d9"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119374"},{"type":"ARTICLE","url":"https://sqlite.org/releaselog/3_54_0.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://sqlite.org/src/info/9cd4f9e920"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sqlite-before-3.54.0-heap-buffer-overflow-via-fts5-fts5dosecuredelete"}],"database_specific":{"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:sqlite:sqlite:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"severity":"High"}}